            <ArticleTitle>[Functional activity of thrombocytes in patients with post-tuberculosis spinal osteochondrosis complicated by pain syndrome].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>7-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It was found that in patients with attenuated tuberculous spondylitis and post-tuberculous vertebral osteochondrosis there was a sharp increase in platelet aggregability and a decrease in their disaggregability at the peak of the pain syndrome. With the therapy followed by relief of the pain syndrome, a rise in the platelet aggregability was significantly less noticeable, without significant changes in their disaggregability.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
